Nested f`` literals in attribute and body holes preserve their literal text.
The outer hole's Go padding can format; a nested literal is not a plain Go
expression, so its own hole spacing stays verbatim. Authored HTML indentation
remains fixed rather than being replaced with canonical nesting indentation.

-- input.gsx --
package p

component Row(who string) {
<div title={f`a @{ f`b @{ who } ` } c`}>
	{f`x @{ f`y @{  who  }` } z`}
</div>
}
-- fmt.golden --
package p

component Row(who string) {
<div title={f`a @{f`b @{ who } `} c`}>
	{f`x @{f`y @{  who  }`} z`}
</div>
}
